<SCENARIO VER="105">
{CREATECG "プレート" "グラフィック\システム\立木三日プレート.gal" "NORMAL" "#1" "180" "380" "600" "1" "100" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{MESON "500"}
<TXSPN>Eiichiro Niimura is the culprit...? Eiichiro Niimura, who should be dead...?<PG>
I see, this is a new viewpoint. If a dead person is the culprit, every puzzling thing may start to become realistic.<PG>
If he used his own death to set off the Megasawa City case and the Motoki-cho murders... Heh, I feel we may arrive at quite an interesting trick.<PG>
The Eiichiro Niimura culprit theory, it is very interesting. A splendid point of view that strikes at a blind spot.<PG>
{}
